course: dictionary
lesson: 5922
title: Married: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Married is an adjective, and it is also the past form of the verb marry. Marry, marries, married and marrying all come from the same word, so when you know one form, you can work out the others.
explain: Read the words around it. «My aunt got married last summer.» Here married means she became a wife or husband. The word summer does not change that, but it tells you when it happened.
explain: Married can also describe people who are wed right now. «Divorce means a married couple end their marriage.» The words couple and marriage show you that married means two people who are husband and wife.
explain: Married to can be an informal phrase meaning very involved in something, such as work. Look at the whole phrase, not just one word, and ask: does the meaning of the phrase fit the sentence?
fact: Married means having a husband or wife.
fact: Married is the past form of marry: marry, marries, married, marrying.
fact: A married couple is two people who are husband and wife.
fact: «Newly married» means married only a short time ago.
fact: Informal: «married to» can mean very involved in something, such as work.
exercise: «My aunt got married last summer.» What does married show here? | She moved to a new house | She lost her wedding ring | She went on holiday | *She became a wife or husband
exercise: Which word is the past form of marry? | marrying | marries | marriage | *married
exercise: «Divorce means a married couple end their marriage.» What is a married couple? | Two children in the same class | *Two people who are husband and wife | Two kings who rule together | Two friends who share a bedroom
test: Which phrase is about two people who got married very recently? | break-up | *newly married | divorce | married couple
test: In «his daughters married kings», what does married mean? | Built a castle | Were sad and lonely | Gathered books | *Became wives of kings
exam: In «My dad is married to his work», what does married to mean? | Hates his job | Works in a wedding shop | Got a new job | *Very involved in his work
